==Old English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|ang|þenċean}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|ang|gem-pro|*þankijaną}}. Cognate with {{cog|ofs|thenka}} ({{cog|fy|tinke}}), {{cog|osx|thenkian}} ({{cog|nds|denken}}), {{cog|odt|thenken}} ({{cog|nl|denken}}), {{cog|goh|denken}} ({{cog|de|denken}}), {{cog|non|þekkja}} ({{cog|gmq-osw|þækkia}}, {{cog|is|þekkja}}), {{cog|got|𐌸𐌰𐌲𐌺𐌾𐌰𐌽}}. All ultimately from {{der|ang|ine-pro|*teng-||to think}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|ang|/ˈθent͡ʃɑn/}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb|þenċan}}

# to [[think]]
#: {{ux|ang|Iċ '''þenċe''', for þȳ iċ eom.|I '''think''', therefore I am.}}
#: {{ux|ang|Ne mage wē '''þenċan''' þæt wē seċġan ne magon.|We cannot '''think''' what we cannot say.}}
#: {{ux|ang|Betere is þæt man '''þenċe''' tō swīðe þonne tō lȳt.|It's better to '''think''' too much than too little.}}

